WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.972
The assessment has two parts.

00:00:01.972 --> 00:00:09.547
First, create analytics dot vw employee department info with employee name, salary, and department name.

00:00:09.547 --> 00:00:12.612
Second, use only that view to calculate the average salary for Sales.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.817
The point is not only the syntax.

00:00:14.817 --> 00:00:21.932
You should also state the grain and explain why the view is a reusable interface.

00:00:21.932 --> 00:00:23.437
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:23.437 --> 00:00:28.542
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:28.542 --> 00:00:33.872
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:33.872 --> 00:00:37.757
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:37.757 --> 00:00:43.872
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:43.872 --> 00:00:49.952
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:49.952 --> 00:00:52.080
not only whether the statement executes.
